//? Title: Nearest Neighbors: Distances, Ties and Exact Matches
//? Subtitle: Choose the metric and aggregation rule before interpreting a prediction
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A new observation can be predicted from nearby labelled examples without fitting a global
parametric function. We inspect tied neighbors on a line, contrast uniform and inverse-distance
regression, and evaluate a fixed Iris classifier on held-out rows. Stable distance and vote ties
are part of a reproducible prediction contract.
)
\toc

> The method

Nearest neighbours stores reference observations and has no learned global parameters.
There is therefore no optimizer or training loop. Tensor distances, selection, weighted
aggregation and training-only scaling implement the full prediction workflow.

For each query, select the k smallest training distances. Regression averages neighbor targets;
classification accumulates class votes. Inverse-distance weighting uses 1/d, except that exact
matches receive all mass when any selected distance is zero:

$$
\widehat f(x)=\frac{\sum_{i\in N_k(x)}w_i y_i}{\sum_{i\in N_k(x)}w_i},\qquad
w_i=1/d_i\ \text{when all selected distances are positive}.
$$
\alttext(A weighted-neighbor regression is the weighted sum of neighbor responses divided by their total weight.)

The tensor helper breaks distance ties by reference-row order and class-vote ties by integer
class ID. Exact matches alone receive equal weight. Otherwise inverse weights use a
squared-distance floor of 1e-20. The Iris example computes standardisation from reference
rows only, then freezes it for all queries. This direct search materialises [Q,N,D]
differences; pairwise distances cost O(QND), followed by selection. Chunk large queries.
High dimension can weaken local distance contrast.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/nearest_neighbors_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/nearest_neighbors_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/nearest_neighbors_concept.tikz > build/nearest_neighbors_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/nearest_neighbors_concept.svg build/nearest_neighbors_concept.dvi > build/nearest_neighbors_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/nearest_neighbors_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
